ib/torchsdk/index.d.ts","size":3312,"sha256":"570b3989d42a28706ddc5c4525f2d571cd73037cae92255172548d847e3cf593","contentType":"application/typescript"},{"path":"lib/torchsdk/tokens.d.ts","size":5266,"sha256":"272708b057697a75bd5e82eaa51bd44b4eb8684cd22f2f10b03d6d011b2e5e87","contentType":"application/typescript"},{"path":"lib/torchsdk/program.js","size":12261,"sha256":"4cf2857228677e8ce3420e2ff4105504832cd5465684b46d63bc04246900ebe2","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"lib/torchsdk/torch_market.json","size":232747,"sha256":"97be148ee5a05bbd04b75dd4e7414fe9968d36ce6dae72461e12300e61109f1c","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":3036,"sha256":"02ffb8c408125abc6127b0edc8bdc80b8794a69d822184a0b55c0f508edcb608","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789033677132,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2801a4aa60aa29b280ea13f6bceb1a24abb9a802f0c8e572833734cae4fdc343","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2801a4aa60aa29b280ea13f6bceb1a24abb9a802f0c8e572833734cae4fdc343","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1779319026800},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":59,"checkedAt":1789033677132},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a coherent Solana DeFi SDK skill, but it deserves user review because it can submit financial transactions and has under-scoped network and supply-chain risks.","dimensions":[{"detail":"SOLANA_RPC_URL is necessary, and SOLANA_PRIVATE_KEY is optional with guidance to use only a disposable controller key. Still, if signing credentials are supplied, the skill can initiate real blockchain transactions, and getToken fetches token metadata from unvalidated creator-controlled URIs.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The SDK is bundled, but the install metadata also allows npm installation of torchsdk@^11.1.0, a mutable version range that can resolve to code not represented by the reviewed artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Read-only mode and optional signing are disclosed, and agent.json separates read, controller, authority, and permissionless actions. However, the skill does not define a tight host permission scope, and runtime behavior includes Solana RPC, wallet signing helpers, SAID/CoinGecko calls, and creator-controlled metadata fetches.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"I found no local persistence, background workers, scheduled tasks, memory modification, or tool hijacking. The main persistent effects are expected on-chain state changes from user-directed protocol transactions and vault/authority operations.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose matches the artifacts: it provides Torch Market read APIs, transaction builders, vault operations, margin lending, short selling, liquidation, migration, and treasury cranks. The concern is not purpose mismatch; it is that this is high-impact financial functionality and some trust claims are broader than the implementation details support.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a DeFi skill that can build and submit real Solana transactions. Prefer read-only/build-only use unless needed, use a fresh disposable controller key rather than any vault authority or high-value wallet, restrict outbound network access where possible, and pin or avoid the optional npm install so reviewed code is what actually runs.","findings":"[TP4] expected: The artifacts do describe permissionless maintenance/crank transactions, so this is not hidden keeper behavior. The 'No keepers' wording is imprecise because some protocol progress depends on permissionless callers rather than privileged keepers.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The 'No stored baselines' claim conflicts with getTreasuryState and type definitions exposing baseline_sol_reserves, baseline_token_reserves, and baseline_initialized. This is a documentation and risk-model clarity problem in a financial protocol.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The audit documentation claims a minimal admin surface while also documenting admin-only legacy and short-selling operations. The actions are disclosed elsewhere, so this is not deception, but users should not rely on the broad 'no admin key changes' framing without checking the exact action.\n[SDI-1] expected: The Raydium pool pricing dependency is disclosed as the source of truth. I interpret 'No oracles' as no external oracle feed, not no on-chain market-derived price source.\n[SDI-1] expected: The broader audit documents discuss frontend, API, agent-kit, SAID, and messaging context. That is wider than the short skill description, but agent.json enumerates the corresponding runtime actions and integrations.\n[AR2] expected: The phrase 'without any warning' appears inside a resolved audit finding about silent slippage clamping. It is not an instruction to suppress user warnings or safety guidance.\n[MP3] expected: The cited 'swap instruction' text is ordinary Solana transaction-builder terminology. I found no agent memory manipulation or persistent instruction writing.\n[LP3] unexpected: RPC access and optional signing are expected for the purpose, but the artifacts do not provide a narrowly enforceable permission declaration separating read-only, build-only, and sign/send modes.\n[T09] expected: Fetching token metadata is purpose-aligned, but the implementation fetches creator-controlled URIs without scheme, host, private-IP, redirect, content-type, or body-size validation, creating SSRF exposure in server-side runtimes.\n[T08] unexpected: The mutable npm dependency range is not necessary for the bundled SDK and expands the reviewed code boundary during installation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789033677132}}}}}